{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/345557-changeling-2e-huntsmen-victims-and-survivors","id":345557,"title":"Changeling 2e: Huntsmen, victims and survivors","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-20T01:45:27-08:00","id":345557,"title":"Changeling 2e: Huntsmen, victims and survivors","content":"So there's something that I've been mulling over, which is how the new Huntsmen relate to the core metaphor of Changeling which is often described as &quot;Abuse Survivor not Abuse Victim&quot;.<br /> <br /> I always understood is as the core reason a Changeling was a survivor and not a victim was that the Durance was in the past, the True Fae are still a terrifying threat if they show up, but that's a big if. Mostly they don't show up and a Changeling's core conflict is about building a new life and dealing with the scars from Arcadia.<br /> <br /> Currently we know so little about Huntsmen that I could see them going either way. I could see them flipping the game back to Abuse Victim (as defined by the preceding paragraph).<br /> <br /> So I guess my first question is; are the Huntsmen supposed to be changing the <u>default</u> focus from &quot;moving on&quot; to &quot;worrying about not going back&quot;.<br /> <br /> Assuming the answer is no; my second question is what is being done to prevent the Huntsmen from changing the focus. What do Huntsmen represent in a game about survivors moving forward after they've survived? For example do Huntsmen literally represent how those emotional scars from Arcadia make creating a new life harder? I could think of some great mechanics for that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T05:26:42-08:00","id":345688,"title":"","content":"Recent quotes in the Preliminary Outline thread relevant to this subject:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=342057#post342057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Huntsmen actually sound very interesting, even if before this I saw the archtype they seem to embody as another form or whim of the True Fae. Such as the Arcadian Huntsman in the first edition core book. I dig their concept a lot, but I am concerned by how scary their flexibility of form that's mentioned actually is. It almost makes them scarier than True Fae to consider as enemies, and I feel like that might shift the constant but ephemeral paranoia of first edition to very real and claustrophobic nightmares in a Changeling's life.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=342070#post342070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm basically somewhat concerned the Huntsmen might overshadow the True Fae as an ephemeral background presence that incites not always justified paranoia and madness. Because instead they'll be enforcing very real and claustrophobic concerns that Changelings have to always live with. They can still play into the difficulty Changelings are supposed to have with distinguishing reality from dreams and not letting their nightmares suffocate their view of the world, but...<br /> <br /> To me, it could very easily miss the mark of what the antagonists of Changeling The Lost and some of its themes are about, depending on how their concept is explored. They make me think more of Demon than Changeling, or how a friend of mine I just discussed this with put it, &quot;they're the Angels of Changeling The Lost&quot;. Now, I might be biased, because while I love Demon The Descent, I am unable to get into character as one without the unease and anxiety doing bad things to me. That, and I love the shit out of the True Fae as antagonists in the World Of Darkness period.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=342357#post342357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably toning down presence of Huntsmen would be a sensible approach. Occassional, but real threat, not bogeymen that are main concern. Simply, there should be a sort of balance.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=342818#post342818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I fear the Huntsmen eclipsing the True Fae as the defining antagonists (behind the scenes and not) of Changeling The Lost. Say what you will, but to me, the Gentry have always felt like the one grand enemy of the Lost behind the curtains. Sometimes they're not there at all, sometimes they're pulling strings behind it, and rarely they pull it open and present themselves as actors in the play.<br /> <br /> Changeling The Lost is primarily about the Lost themselves, of course. But as their main opposition, the Fae are very important. (In fact, we've been told in this very thread they're in the Storytelling chapter and not the antagonists one.)</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=345025#post345025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having thought a few days on this, I'm interested in icons. It seems like a cool idea, and not just for building off the &quot;personal myth&quot; idea that I'm also really digging. The thought of little bits that tore off of the Changeling in the Hedge forming into ties to that Changeling's legend is very cool, and an appropriate means of tracking the Lost. I wonder what other properties they might have and what other uses they might serve.<br /> <br /> That said, I do admit to having a possibly unfounded concern about their property of forever reappearing in the Hedge. Some executions of that idea with the Huntsmen could tip the tone from &quot;I can never know if I'm safe,&quot; to &quot;I know I'm never safe.&quot; Not jumping to conclusions here, just mentioning initial thoughts that strike me from the exceptionally little that's yet been mentioned.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T12:17:48-08:00","id":347598,"title":"","content":"Well of course we can always set the tone on how we choose to play the Game. The Huntsmen Chronicle can be a game changer, but doesn't necessarily mess with the theme unless you allow it. Personally i look at changelings as both &quot; Abuse victims &amp; Survivors&quot;. Trying to make a new life for yourself is hard enough, but who says nothing else will happen to you while your doing so? I look at it as a added Conflict, second to if a True Fae arrived to come for you. Not All Changelings are trying to fix there lives to be normal either mind you. Hence the Summer Courts &quot;Bridge Burners&quot; and such, it's all about how you approach this. I've come to picture the Huntsmen as like a privateer/loyalist Changling with high wyrd. Not as powerful as a true fae but powerful enough to wreck a motley or have a court tense if not paranoid. Not enough to overshadow the True Fae, but enough to have the changelings equally scared.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>&quot;I am a daydreamer and a Night thinker.&quot;~</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1820-nightout","name":"Nightout","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T03:03:53-08:00","id":350548,"title":"","content":"Reading now Equinox Road I would ask if the Huntsmen so do not steal reason for True Fae to kidnap humans in the first place? One of main source of Legend on what the Fae thrive is escape and Hunt for their once slaves. If Huntsman take the changelings on themsleves, what is, narrativle speaking, a conflict for True Fae?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T05:15:26-08:00","id":350571,"title":"","content":"One Note: As far we know, the True Fae aren\u00b4t always malevolent (that would be <i>boring </i>and predictable); is it impossible to see one of the Others trying to help a motley just because he/she can?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T06:55:31-08:00","id":350635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Reading now Equinox Road I would ask if the Huntsmen so do not steal reason for True Fae to kidnap humans in the first place? One of main source of Legend on what the Fae thrive is escape and Hunt for their once slaves. If Huntsman take the changelings on themsleves, what is, narrativle speaking, a conflict for True Fae? </div> </div> </div>That's why True Fae bother to do it usually themselves, but if they cannot be arsed to do that personally because they have more 'pressing' issues like a Feud with another True Fae, getting new manservants or punishing escaped ones is enough secondary matter to leave it in hands of hired help.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T09:37:12-08:00","id":350705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/345557-changeling-2e-huntsmen-victims-and-survivors?p=350571#post350571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One Note: As far we know, the True Fae aren\u00b4t always malevolent (that would be <i>boring </i>and predictable); is it impossible to see one of the Others trying to help a motley just because he/she can?</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of the time Kindly One will only help you if you are fighting with it's rival. But he will help you then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T10:15:38-08:00","id":350736,"title":"","content":"Or it does that for shits and giggles just because so. True Fae have too distorted mindset to readily classify their behavior.<br /> <br /> Though, rivalry can be still a factor. I have 'good' True Fae who masquerades as a lesser forest god and supports (read: uses as pawns) mortals and Changelings alike against minions of his rival. He sustains himself on the feud and does not abduct mortals to his Realm, so some of those who realize his identity prefer to look the other way in hopes he won't change his modus operandi. And there is this fact his rival does abduct mortals rather frequently (and has a cult formed around the fact it rewards its mortal minions with possessions of those abducted, such behavior being part of its legend). So, better to cooperate with the 'lesser evil'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":2918,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","user":"Kat","date":". 12-26-2014, 01:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T12:13:17-08:00","id":350825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/345557-changeling-2e-huntsmen-victims-and-survivors?p=350635#post350635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's why True Fae bother to do it usually themselves, but if they cannot be arsed to do that personally because they have more 'pressing' issues like a Feud with another True Fae, getting new manservants or punishing escaped ones is enough secondary matter to leave it in hands of hired help.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Another possibility covers True Fae who won't (or can't) just snatch up anybody at any time they please. There are examples given about mortals who were taken because they'd violated some arcane stricture, who'd inadvertently wandered into reach of one of the Others, or who'd struck a bargain (implicit or explicit) with one. There's an implication in those cases that the Stranger either couldn't get them any other way or <i>could</i> but <i>wouldn't</i>.*<br /> <br /> * Difficulty/cost of doing it otherwise, insistence that it happen only a particular way, both, or whatever other rationale.<br /> <br /> Regardless, when a future Changeling is first taken, there may be a special circumstance to it that made it possible, and escape(/release) may find the Gentry in question unable or unwilling to seek or create a new special circumstance for taking back the Lost. In such a case, the Lord or Lady may turn instead to a Huntsman, who is free of these restrictions -- even if perhaps subject to others (we don't know enough about them yet, but I'd expect so).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}